      "evidence": "template/scripts/local_workspace.py:172 raises `foreign active worktree; owner must act: {item}`. It names no owner and gives no chgrp/chmod command. `audit(repair=True)` calls `checkout` first, so `admit_repairing` (diff lines 330-345) propagates this message. `shared_workspace._admit_local_source_repairing` wraps it unchanged in SharedWorkspaceError. tests/test_local_workspace.py `test_preflight_admission_refuses_another_accounts_task_without_repair` asserts only the regex 'foreign active worktree'. Foreign files inside an own worktree go through the findings path, which may be compliant, but the whole-worktree foreign case is not.",
      "id": "foreign-admission-refusal-lacks-owner-and-command",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The spec requires a foreign-owned path to be refused with the owner and the exact chgrp/chmod repair command. When `admit_repairing` reaches a foreign worktree, it raises the generic checkout message instead. The new test only asserts that generic text."
